## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical guardrail implementation and rollback in Azure, focusing on private endpoints and storage exposure controls.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy initiatives
- Private Endpoint and Private DNS for SQL
- Storage account publicNetworkAccess controls
- Post-deploy validation and rapid rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Post-deploy validation sketch (Node.js)
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const { StorageManagementClient } = require("@azure/arm-storage");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const subscriptionId = "<sub-id>";
const client = new StorageManagementClient(credential, subscriptionId);
async function checkStoragePublicAccess(rg, name) {
  const acc = await client.storageAccounts.getProperties(rg, name);
  return acc?.properties?.networkAcls?.publicNetworkAccess !== "Enabled";
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this in a dev environment before production rollout?
- What logs/alerts would you configure to catch violations early, and how would you automate rollback if the last-good template isn’t found?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess hands-on orchestration across Azure components during incidents, focusing on tenant isolation, automated rollback safety, and auditable controls.

## Key Concepts
- UEBA-driven automation (Defender for Cloud/Sentinel)
- Per-tenant network isolation (NSG, Private Endpoint)
- Key Vault key rotation and re-encryption
- Token revocation and Conditional Access control
- Canary-based rollback mechanisms
- Centralized auditing and alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator snippet
async function quarantineTenant(tenantId){
  await applyPerTenantNSG(tenantId);
  await rotateKeyVaultKeys(tenantId);
  await revokeTokensAndDisableCA(tenantId);
  await rollbackToLastGoodRelease(tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of basic network security controls in Azure and practical rollout/rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Private Link and Private Endpoints
- Storage Account network rules (default deny)
- Azure Policy enforcement
- Rollback and test strategies

## Code Example
```bicep
param storageAccountName string
param vnetSubnetId string
resource pe 'Microsoft.Network/privateEndpoints@2020-11-01' = {
  name: '${storageAccountName}-pe'
  location: resourceGroup().location
  properties: {
    subnet: { id: vnetSubnetId }
    privateLinkServiceConnections: [
      {
        name: 'storageBlob'
        properties: {
          privateLinkServiceId: '/subscriptions/.../resourceGroups/.../providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/${storageAccountName}'
          groupIds: [ 'blob' ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
        { "not": { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/privateEndpointConnections", "exists": true } }
        }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify the guardrail in CI/CD pipelines?
- How would you extend to multi-region deployments and private DNS considerations?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design an automated, policy-driven containment workflow for PayPal/Stripe-scale apps across regions, including rapid isolation, credential hygiene, and deterministic rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Defender for Cloud alerts and automation triggers
- Azure Locks and policy gates for containment
- Key Vault secret rotation and SPN credential management
- Canary testing and automatic rollback orchestration
- Incident reporting and post-incident review

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch for containment automation
async function containBreach(alert) {
  await applyLock(alert.affectedResources);
  await rotateSecrets(alert.secretsToRotate);
  const ok = await runCanaryTests(alert.canaryPlan);
  if (!ok) await rollbackToBaseline(alert);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the rollback under load and ensure data integrity?
- Which metrics determine abort vs. continue during containment and rollback?
